ENTRY            21311   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
SUBENT        21311001   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                 11         19
TITLE      Observation of doubly radiative neutron capture by
            3He
AUTHOR     (M.Suffert, R.Berthollet)
INSTITUTE  (2FR STR,2FR ILL)
REFERENCE  (J,NP/A,318,54,1979)
FACILITY   (REAC,2FR ILL) ILL high-flux reactor
INC-SOURCE (THCOL) H22 thermal neutron guide at the reactor
INC-SPECT  Total flux of 2.6E+09 +/- 0.1E+09 neutrons/s (thermal
            equivalent).
SAMPLE     Pure helium-3 gas in a 90 mm long gas target at 2 bar
DETECTOR   (NAICR) Two NaI(Tl) detectors (25 cm diam. and 30 cm
            long), each surrounded, except for the front side,
            by a thick plastic scintillator.
           The NaI(Tl) detectors were peak efficiency calibrated
            by means of the 3H(p,g)4He reaction at Ep=1.0 MeV.
METHOD     (COINC) Standard slow-fast coincidence arrangement
HISTORY    (19800206C) CN.
           (19800213E)
           (20260311A) On. Major revisions in 002-003.
ENDBIB              19
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           22
SUBENT        21311002   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                  5          6
REACTION   (2-HE-3(N,G)2-HE-4,,DA,,4PI/SPA)
METHOD     Detection of 20.6 MeV gamma-rays
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Mainly due to detection geometry chosen for
            maximum efficiency
STATUS     (TABLE,,M.Suffert+,J,NP/A,318,54,1979) Text (p.56)
HISTORY    (20260311A) On. REACTION updated.
ENDBIB               6
NOCOMMON             0          0
DATA                 4          1
EN-DUMMY   ANG        DATA       DATA-ERR
EV         ADEG       MICRO-B    MICRO-B
 0.0253     45.        60.        12.
ENDDATA              3
ENDSUBENT           14
SUBENT        21311003   20260311   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                  6         11
REACTION   (2-HE-3(N,G)2-HE-4,,SIG,,SPA/MSC)
METHOD     Detection of two gamma-rays with an angle of 90 deg
            between the detectors and assuming an angular
            correlation of 1+(cos)**2 between the two gamma-rays.
CORRECTION Corrected for
            - coincidence efficiency,
            - background,
            - count loss due to low-energy cutoff at Eg=2.6 MeV
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) No information on the source of uncertainty
STATUS     (TABLE,,M.Suffert+,J,NP/A,318,54,1979) Text (p.61)
HISTORY    (20260311A) On. REACTION updated. E-MAX deleted.
ENDBIB              11
NOCOMMON             0          0
DATA                 3          1
EN-DUMMY   DATA       DATA-ERR
EV         MICRO-B    MICRO-B
 0.0253     17.        5.
ENDDATA              3
ENDSUBENT           19
ENDENTRY             3
